#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166663 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166825 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "99f2c276-2eb0-5fe9-b46d-6cf30547a96e" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Z-Score for a Given Probability Using Interval Bisection"}] :question/id #uuid "a2b50673-6a4f-5e64-ae16-fdce0819637e" :question/math-academy-id "e-8526" :question/problem "Approximate the value of $z$ such that $P(Z \\leq z) = 0.1450$ using interval bisection.\n\n| $z$ | $\\, 0.05 \\,$ | $\\, 0.06 \\,$ | $\\, 0.07 \\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\, -1.0 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1469 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1446 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1423 \\,$ |\n| $\\, -0.9 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1711 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1685 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1660 \\,$ |\n| $\\, -0.8 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1977 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1949 \\,$ | $\\, 0.1922 \\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the two numbers in the table that $0.1450$ lies between. These numbers are $0.1446$ and $0.1469.$ So, we have the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.1446 & <0.1450<0.1469\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above inequality in terms of $\\Phi,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-1.06) & <Φ(z)<Φ(-1.05).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, using interval bisection, we can approximate $z$ as\n\n$$\nz \\approx \\dfrac{-1.06 + (-1.05)}{2} = -1.055.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166664 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166826 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a54afd65-a69e-52dd-84eb-7cf936773678" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Percentage Points Table To Find the Z-Score for a Given Probability"}] :question/id #uuid "d1e64fae-04ef-5c7d-9bb0-e81cf06bb672" :question/math-academy-id "e-8528" :question/problem "The table below gives the values of $\\Phi^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p = \\Phi(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z \\leq z) = 0.60.$\n\n| $\\quad p \\quad$ | $0.60$ | $0.65$ | $0.70$ | $0.75$ | $0.80$ | $0.85$ | $0.90$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\Phi^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,0.2533\\,$ | $\\,0.3853\\,$ | $\\,0.5244\\,$ | $\\,0.6745\\,$ | $\\,0.8416\\,$ | $\\,1.0364\\,$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, we express the given information in terms of $\\Phi{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\le z) & =0.60 \\\\ Φ(z) & =0.60\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we are looking for the value of $z$ such that\n\n$$\nz = \\Phi^{-1} (0.60).\n$$\n\nWe look for the column in the table that corresponds to $p = 0.60,$ and we find that\n\n$$\np = 0.60 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad \\Phi^{-1}(p) = 0.2533.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nz =  \\Phi^{-1}(0.60) = 0.2533.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166673 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166831 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8742ad90-1d33-5b56-a83f-8edd7f2f5aef" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Percentage Points Table and Symmetry To Find the Z-Score for a Given Probability"}] :question/id #uuid "a29f1f2c-104a-53aa-ad55-0c6abde0a359" :question/math-academy-id "e-8590" :question/problem "The table below gives the values of $\\Phi^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p = \\Phi(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z \\leq z) = 0.20.$\n\n| $\\quad p \\quad$ | $0.65$ | $0.70$ | $0.75$ | $0.80$ | $0.85$ | $0.90$ | $0.95$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\Phi^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,0.3853\\,$ | $\\,0.5244\\,$ | $\\,0.6745\\,$ | $\\,0.8416\\,$ | $\\,1.0364\\,$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "From the table, notice that\n\n$$\nP(Z\\leq 0.8416 ) = 0.80.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(Z\\geq 0.8416 ) = 1 - 0.80 = 0.20.\n$$\n\nBy the symmetry of the standard normal distribution, we have\n\n$$\n\\Phi(-0.8416) = 0.20.\n$$\n\n![](images/2b/2be6ef2420c8789a0ff94f4f9540533af4134690ebe0c04c50eb02f358dfa266.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-0.8416) & =0.20 \\\\ P(Z\\le -0.8416) & =0.20.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the required value of $z$ is $-0.8416.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489210 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166826 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a54afd65-a69e-52dd-84eb-7cf936773678" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Percentage Points Table To Find the Z-Score for a Given Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20277f6b-6957-5eff-974f-9f54920b0c35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.0902" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488536} {:answer/id #uuid "3adfc64b-e003-5630-aeb9-acf68f203a8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.2905" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488591} {:answer/id #uuid "69010aff-3ab9-5d0e-be44-6b0951a67112" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.8330" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488674} {:answer/id #uuid "cd659ed7-8f4b-51cf-bea7-2ad403c7e94f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.1903" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488889} {:answer/id #uuid "ff819ae6-c0b0-5dab-9404-30f76f981bf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5758" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489015}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3adfc64b-e003-5630-aeb9-acf68f203a8d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.2905" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488591} :answer-field/id #uuid "44c234c3-a395-5292-a122-e598d1b5e13a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489055}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "498c3c25-8224-532d-867c-1bb7c9c3d797" :question/math-academy-id "q-164331" :question/problem "The table below gives the values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.9995.$\n\n| $p$ | $\\,0.900\\,$ | $\\,0.950\\,$ | $\\,0.975\\,$ | $\\,0.990\\,$ | $\\,0.995\\,$ | $\\,0.999\\,$ | $\\,0.9995\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ | $\\,1.9600\\,$ | $\\,2.3263\\,$ | $\\,2.5758\\,$ | $\\,3.0902\\,$ | $\\,3.2905\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, we express the given information in terms of $Φ:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\le z) & =0.9995 \\\\ Φ(z) & =0.9995\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we are looking for the value of $z$ such that\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.9995).\n$$\n\nWe look for the column in the table that corresponds to $p=0.9995,$ and we find that\n\n$$\np=0.9995\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(p)=3.2905.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.9995)=3.2905.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489215 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166831 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8742ad90-1d33-5b56-a83f-8edd7f2f5aef" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Percentage Points Table and Symmetry To Find the Z-Score for a Given Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "64f67ed2-d6ad-582c-9058-5742f4394ed3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.2816" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488662} {:answer/id #uuid "6ff373d7-66ef-5f4e-85b7-ea2ef57bdfc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3.0902" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488692} {:answer/id #uuid "95f8d5ee-929e-5317-8d0a-133e273ac264" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.0902" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488773} {:answer/id #uuid "e8a0e8c1-effb-5b17-a58a-5cba623c360a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.2816" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488959} {:answer/id #uuid "e9cee8aa-e3d3-56b7-97e8-19c302c5d275" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.3263" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488961}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64f67ed2-d6ad-582c-9058-5742f4394ed3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.2816" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488662} :answer-field/id #uuid "36d38cd0-7f8a-5483-a8b4-00b891bc2efd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489048}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4d1937b2-4611-58ce-a050-d85b88c9c4df" :question/math-academy-id "q-164332" :question/problem "The table below gives the values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.10.$\n\n| $p$ | $\\,0.900\\,$ | $\\,0.950\\,$ | $\\,0.975\\,$ | $\\,0.990\\,$ | $\\,0.995\\,$ | $\\,0.999\\,$ | $\\,0.9995\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ | $\\,1.9600\\,$ | $\\,2.3263\\,$ | $\\,2.5758\\,$ | $\\,3.0902\\,$ | $\\,3.2905\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "From the table, notice that\n\n$$\nP(Z\\le 1.2816)=0.90.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(Z\\ge 1.2816)=1-0.90=0.10.\n$$\n\nBy the symmetry of the standard normal distribution, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(-1.2816)=0.10.\n$$\n\n![](images/fe/feb06180815c7ae83a5034ff8933700fd5778c9ab0bfba54fe95bb67104662b7.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-1.2816) & =0.10 \\\\ P(Z\\le -1.2816) & =0.10.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required value of $z$ is $-1.2816.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284474 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166831 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8742ad90-1d33-5b56-a83f-8edd7f2f5aef" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Percentage Points Table and Symmetry To Find the Z-Score for a Given Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "11f299df-5afb-5251-a8b9-07729da3e2c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.3263" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281862} {:answer/id #uuid "31d8df3e-2326-5360-84b5-195a0b825710" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.2816" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282138} {:answer/id #uuid "61ff013c-5300-5bfb-8245-66276fc6bd84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.0902" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282524} {:answer/id #uuid "63e35f0e-2deb-5946-85ed-4b07144fa947" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.3263" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282549} {:answer/id #uuid "e2198a84-ee66-539d-94ae-5bd4c1e15003" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.2816" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186283662}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "11f299df-5afb-5251-a8b9-07729da3e2c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.3263" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281862} :answer-field/id #uuid "a28c3d6d-1eab-598e-9c73-3198876e6a3e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284212}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "85c72120-a302-5186-9506-8f0d0fa22ef4" :question/math-academy-id "q-164333" :question/problem "The table below gives the values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z>z)=0.01.$\n\n| $p$ | $\\,0.900\\,$ | $\\,0.950\\,$ | $\\,0.975\\,$ | $\\,0.990\\,$ | $\\,0.995\\,$ | $\\,0.999\\,$ | $\\,0.9995\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ | $\\,1.9600\\,$ | $\\,2.3263\\,$ | $\\,2.5758\\,$ | $\\,3.0902\\,$ | $\\,3.2905\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, we express the given information in terms of $Φ,$ using the complement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z>z) & =0.01 \\\\ 1-P(Z\\le z) & =0.01 \\\\ 1-Φ(z) & =0.01 \\\\ Φ(z) & =1-0.01 \\\\ Φ(z) & =0.99\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we are looking for the value of $z$ such that\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.99).\n$$\n\nWe look for the column in the table that corresponds to $p=0.99,$ and we find that\n\n$$\np=0.99\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(p)=2.3263.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.99)=2.3263.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302420 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166825 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "99f2c276-2eb0-5fe9-b46d-6cf30547a96e" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Z-Score for a Given Probability Using Interval Bisection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7696548-3764-50fe-9203-76d3a45cede8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.625" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301033}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7696548-3764-50fe-9203-76d3a45cede8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.625" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301033} :answer-field/id #uuid "746728e1-7f30-5503-98b8-df427de87a07" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301587}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f974be1b-50fc-5e85-a97a-26d0236743e8" :question/math-academy-id "q-328306" :question/problem "| $z$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,1.5\\,$ | $\\,0.9345\\,$ | $\\,0.9357\\,$ | $\\,0.9370\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.6\\,$ | $\\,0.9463\\,$ | $\\,0.9474\\,$ | $\\,0.9484\\,$ |\n| $\\,1.7\\,$ | $\\,0.9564\\,$ | $\\,0.9573\\,$ | $\\,0.9582\\,$ |\n\nApproximate the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.9480$ using interval bisection and the above table.\n\n$z≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the two numbers in the table that $0.9480$ lies between. These numbers are $0.9474$ and $0.9484.$ So, we have the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.9474 & <0.9480<0.9484\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above inequality in terms of $Φ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(1.62) & <Φ(z)<Φ(1.63).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, using interval bisection, we can approximate $z$ as\n\n$$\nz≈\\frac{1.62+1.63}{2}=1.625.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489223 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166825 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "99f2c276-2eb0-5fe9-b46d-6cf30547a96e" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Z-Score for a Given Probability Using Interval Bisection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92d9b53a-882b-5842-85be-c8c6715c1bf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.555" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488765}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92d9b53a-882b-5842-85be-c8c6715c1bf0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.555" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488765} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e3569f9-57c5-5dcb-ba38-28e922d55560" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489072}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "5f71a427-dbf6-5a8f-8911-889945fe6b51" :question/math-academy-id "q-328307" :question/problem "| $z$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-1.6\\,$ | $\\,0.0495\\,$ | $\\,0.0485\\,$ | $\\,0.0475\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.5\\,$ | $\\,0.0606\\,$ | $\\,0.0594\\,$ | $\\,0.0582\\,$ |\n| $\\,-1.4\\,$ | $\\,0.0735\\,$ | $\\,0.0721\\,$ | $\\,0.0708\\,$ |\n\nApproximate the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.0600$ using interval bisection and the above table\n\n$z≈$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the two numbers in the table that $0.0600$ lies between. These numbers are $0.0594$ and $0.0606.$ So, we have the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.0594 & <0.0600<0.0606\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above inequality in terms of $Φ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-1.56) & <Φ(z)<Φ(-1.55).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, using interval bisection, we can approximate $z$ as\n\n$$\nz≈\\frac{-1.56+(-1.55)}{2}=-1.555.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489271 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166825 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "99f2c276-2eb0-5fe9-b46d-6cf30547a96e" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Z-Score for a Given Probability Using Interval Bisection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "338b4414-16ee-56e9-871a-17c47c61bf78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.525" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "338b4414-16ee-56e9-871a-17c47c61bf78" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.525" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488579} :answer-field/id #uuid "f8b471bf-ec68-521e-9a36-666090833190" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489163}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cfe7c3c3-ab90-5b66-a414-95dcb308c4a8" :question/math-academy-id "q-328316" :question/problem "| $z$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ | $\\,0.03\\,$ |\n| -