1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.20.$ Use the table below and do not round your answer.\n\n| $\\,p\\,$ | $0.10$ | $0.15$ | $0.20$ | $0.25$ | $0.30$ | $0.35$ | $0.40$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,-1.2816\\,$ | $\\,-1.0364\\,$ | $\\,-0.8416\\,$ | $\\,-0.6745\\,$ | $\\,-0.5244\\,$ | $\\,-0.3853\\,$ | $\\,-0.2533\\,$ |\n\n$z=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we express the given information in terms of $Φ:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\le z) & =0.20 \\\\ Φ(z) & =0.20\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we are looking for the value of $z$ such that\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.20).\n$$\n\nWe look for the column in the table that corresponds to $p=0.20,$ and we find that\n\n$$\np=0.20\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(p)=-0.8416.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.20)=-0.8416.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489191 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166826 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a54afd65-a69e-52dd-84eb-7cf936773678" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Percentage Points Table To Find the Z-Score for a Given Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9546136f-9e31-5ec3-bbbd-32bc3c2578d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.2533" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488770}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9546136f-9e31-5ec3-bbbd-32bc3c2578d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.2533" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488770} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e05090a-954b-5985-81a1-91310ca48f77" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489071}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2325fcf7-3419-5c2a-84d5-5bfca9cad5a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-328466" :question/problem "The table below gives the values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.40.$ Use the table below and do not round your answer.\n\n| $\\,p\\,$ | $0.10$ | $0.15$ | $0.20$ | $0.25$ | $0.30$ | $0.35$ | $0.40$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,-1.2816\\,$ | $\\,-1.0364\\,$ | $\\,-0.8416\\,$ | $\\,-0.6745\\,$ | $\\,-0.5244\\,$ | $\\,-0.3853\\,$ | $\\,-0.2533\\,$ |\n\n$z=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we express the given information in terms of $Φ:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\le z) & =0.40 \\\\ Φ(z) & =0.40\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we are looking for the value of $z$ such that\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.40).\n$$\n\nWe look for the column in the table that corresponds to $p=0.40,$ and we find that\n\n$$\np=0.40\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(p)=-0.2533.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.40)=-0.2533.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489251 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166831 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8742ad90-1d33-5b56-a83f-8edd7f2f5aef" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Percentage Points Table and Symmetry To Find the Z-Score for a Given Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "107b6af3-b6a7-5e28-a4ad-8e9b12ea92b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.96" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488508}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "107b6af3-b6a7-5e28-a4ad-8e9b12ea92b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.96" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488508} :answer-field/id #uuid "9bf92771-7c95-5c4e-a5e9-de264eeed978" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489103}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9ffb7646-1918-5230-b400-64576248fe40" :question/math-academy-id "q-328474" :question/problem "The table below gives the values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.025.$ Use the table below and do not round your answer.\n\n| $p$ | $\\,0.900\\,$ | $\\,0.950\\,$ | $\\,0.975\\,$ | $\\,0.990\\,$ | $\\,0.995\\,$ | $\\,0.999\\,$ | $\\,0.9995\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ | $\\,1.9600\\,$ | $\\,2.3263\\,$ | $\\,2.5758\\,$ | $\\,3.0902\\,$ | $\\,3.2905\\,$ |\n\n$z=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "From the table, notice that\n\n$$\nP(Z\\le 1.96)=0.975.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(Z\\ge 1.96)=1-0.975=0.025.\n$$\n\nBy the symmetry of the standard normal distribution, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(-1.96)=0.025.\n$$\n\n![](images/e4/e46e28a748745da14c260af2c39c7c10983b40476c57d8d75a51f0390d2359d2.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-1.96) & =0.025 \\\\ P(Z\\le -1.96) & =0.025.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required value of $z$ is $-1.96.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489190 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166831 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8742ad90-1d33-5b56-a83f-8edd7f2f5aef" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Percentage Points Table and Symmetry To Find the Z-Score for a Given Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c781b62-786a-5c02-b4cc-f00667fc5101" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6745" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488497}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c781b62-786a-5c02-b4cc-f00667fc5101" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.6745" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488497} :answer-field/id #uuid "11eb93d2-4ed3-55c1-b04f-9715439b2be7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489029}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "222d3245-c08e-59e6-abe7-30dbec831345" :question/math-academy-id "q-328480" :question/problem "The table below gives the values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z>z)=0.25.$ Use the table below and do not round your answer.\n\n| $\\,p\\,$ | $0.65$ | $0.70$ | $0.75$ | $0.80$ | $0.85$ | $0.90$ | $0.95$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,0.3853\\,$ | $\\,0.5244\\,$ | $\\,0.6745\\,$ | $\\,0.8416\\,$ | $\\,1.0364\\,$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ |\n\n$z=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "First, we express the given information in terms of $Φ,$ using the complement:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z>z) & =0.25 \\\\ 1-P(Z\\le z) & =0.25 \\\\ 1-Φ(z) & =0.25 \\\\ Φ(z) & =1-0.25 \\\\ Φ(z) & =0.75\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we are looking for the value of $z$ such that\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.75).\n$$\n\nWe look for the column in the table that corresponds to $p=0.75,$ and we find that\n\n$$\np=0.75\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(p)=0.6745.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.75)=0.6745.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489202 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166825 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "99f2c276-2eb0-5fe9-b46d-6cf30547a96e" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Z-Score for a Given Probability Using Interval Bisection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e2bbdda-76fd-5310-bdfc-4fbc02785431" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.705" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488569} {:answer/id #uuid "920f923d-dc48-5a5e-9fca-90f668b81d01" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.605" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488761} {:answer/id #uuid "a5315bab-1d11-5e74-9023-48df546c6cb5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.815" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488797} {:answer/id #uuid "b6538400-2a27-5611-817a-3228848aae75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.615" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488837} {:answer/id #uuid "f8015e30-90c0-5a27-bd51-791b48ae337a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.715" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488994}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f8015e30-90c0-5a27-bd51-791b48ae337a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0.715" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488994} :answer-field/id #uuid "805fddfe-8f48-5bb5-9c8a-233e7d1d3d22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489086}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2fbf9d75-3749-54f2-b9a0-4aefe7b4559b" :question/math-academy-id "q-96862" :question/problem "Approximate the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.7630$ using interval bisection.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.00\\,$ | $\\,0.01\\,$ | $\\,0.02\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,0.6\\,$ | $\\,0.7257\\,$ | $\\,0.7291\\,$ | $\\,0.7324\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.7\\,$ | $\\,0.7580\\,$ | $\\,0.7611\\,$ | $\\,0.7642\\,$ |\n| $\\,0.8\\,$ | $\\,0.7881\\,$ | $\\,0.7910\\,$ | $\\,0.7939\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the two numbers in the table that $0.7630$ lies between. These numbers are $0.7611$ and $0.7642.$ So, we have the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.7611 & <0.7630<0.7642\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above inequality in terms of $Φ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(0.71) & <Φ(z)<Φ(0.72).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, using interval bisection, we can approximate $z$ as\n\n$$\nz≈\\frac{0.71+0.72}{2}=0.715.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489270 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166825 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "99f2c276-2eb0-5fe9-b46d-6cf30547a96e" :knowledge-point/title "Estimating the Z-Score for a Given Probability Using Interval Bisection"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "253fbccc-a2c8-55cb-9e16-0c7421cd1d12" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.455" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488547} {:answer/id #uuid "65666da5-14b2-5993-8bc2-0526aae204af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.565" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488663} {:answer/id #uuid "baa6de8f-284d-53b5-a4b5-5d8832406ae0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.365" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488845} {:answer/id #uuid "e67b84dd-1d8d-5eb0-bda0-e01f8685277d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.545" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488951} {:answer/id #uuid "ecbf931d-740e-5b29-8d5d-f8a78af98be9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.555" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488969}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ecbf931d-740e-5b29-8d5d-f8a78af98be9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-0.555" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488969} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb366ba9-396c-5a42-bdaf-db347d7da9e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489133}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cf9b9ee0-bd15-54c0-b3c4-9825b1263a05" :question/math-academy-id "q-96864" :question/problem "Approximate the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.2900$ using interval bisection.\n\n| $z$ | $\\,0.05\\,$ | $\\,0.06\\,$ | $\\,0.07\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\,-0.5\\,$ | $\\,0.2912\\,$ | $\\,0.2877\\,$ | $\\,0.2843\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.4\\,$ | $\\,0.3264\\,$ | $\\,0.3228\\,$ | $\\,0.3192\\,$ |\n| $\\,-0.3\\,$ | $\\,0.3632\\,$ | $\\,0.3594\\,$ | $\\,0.3557\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the two numbers in the table that $0.2900$ lies between. These numbers are $0.2877$ and $0.2912.$ So, we have the following inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}0.2877 & <0.2900<0.2912\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWriting the above inequality in terms of $Φ,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-0.56) & <Φ(z)<Φ(-0.55).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, using interval bisection, we can approximate $z$ as\n\n$$\nz≈\\frac{-0.56+(-0.55)}{2}=-0.555.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489272 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166826 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a54afd65-a69e-52dd-84eb-7cf936773678" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Percentage Points Table To Find the Z-Score for a Given Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ec30051-b0f4-5569-896b-0881dc28eda4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.6449" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488571} {:answer/id #uuid "907f9238-2918-58cd-9a06-3b899ae2f9e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5758" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488757} {:answer/id #uuid "ae1660cd-36d2-5645-8a6f-328abac9e59b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.3263" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488817} {:answer/id #uuid "d4fd2043-1fad-56f6-912c-e1d9568bb630" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.9600" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488907} {:answer/id #uuid "e63d4436-06b2-5794-a1a0-a90f532c1812" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.2905" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488950}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "907f9238-2918-58cd-9a06-3b899ae2f9e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5758" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488757} :answer-field/id #uuid "4fe11fc7-6fbb-5dee-bf1e-d62730e9a509" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489061}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d124118c-140f-52f2-b4ac-16dbd784c35b" :question/math-academy-id "q-96933" :question/problem "The table below gives the values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.995.$\n\n| $p$ | $\\,0.900\\,$ | $\\,0.950\\,$ | $\\,0.975\\,$ | $\\,0.990\\,$ | $\\,0.995\\,$ | $\\,0.999\\,$ | $\\,0.9995\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ | $\\,1.9600\\,$ | $\\,2.3263\\,$ | $\\,2.5758\\,$ | $\\,3.0902\\,$ | $\\,3.2905\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, we express the given information in terms of $Φ:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\le z) & =0.995 \\\\ Φ(z) & =0.995\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we are looking for the value of $z$ such that\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.995).\n$$\n\nWe look for the column in the table that corresponds to $p=0.995,$ and we find that\n\n$$\np=0.995\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(p)=2.5758.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.995)=2.5758.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360725 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166826 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a54afd65-a69e-52dd-84eb-7cf936773678" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Percentage Points Table To Find the Z-Score for a Given Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d57011b-7bdb-5d6e-9649-8309bae4efcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.0902" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358007} {:answer/id #uuid "acee74f9-0907-5d64-acce-0158fc8e8396" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5758" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359245} {:answer/id #uuid "bf99f561-0110-5798-b118-469c2b77aa24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.0929" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359428} {:answer/id #uuid "d2187c6a-044f-5c3b-b9b8-1b39abd32e13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.3263" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359588} {:answer/id #uuid "d61fb95f-1972-5160-a45d-84a43d6c34b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.2905" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186359627}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1d57011b-7bdb-5d6e-9649-8309bae4efcd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.0902" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186358007} :answer-field/id #uuid "a4c3987d-8d53-5e98-8e73-e2189f9639df" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186360282}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bbb237cf-844c-54a3-a031-530faf349f3d" :question/math-academy-id "q-96936" :question/problem "The table below gives the values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.999.$\n\n| $\\,p\\,$ | $0.900$ | $0.950$ | $0.975$ | $0.990$ | $0.995$ | $0.999$ | $0.9995$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,1.2816\\,$ | $\\,1.6449\\,$ | $\\,1.9600\\,$ | $\\,2.3263\\,$ | $\\,2.5758\\,$ | $\\,3.0902\\,$ | $\\,3.2905\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "First, we express the given information in terms of $Φ:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(Z\\le z) & =0.999 \\\\ Φ(z) & =0.999\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we are looking for the value of $z$ such that\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.999).\n$$\n\nWe look for the column in the table that corresponds to $p=0.999,$ and we find that\n\n$$\np=0.999\\,⇒\\,{Φ}^{-1}(p)=3.0902.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nz={Φ}^{-1}(0.999)=3.0902.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186489278 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186166831 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8742ad90-1d33-5b56-a83f-8edd7f2f5aef" :knowledge-point/title "Using a Percentage Points Table and Symmetry To Find the Z-Score for a Given Probability"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2a163fc6-b329-585d-a1b9-5b8e8a43d026" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.6449" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488559} {:answer/id #uuid "39268e53-d205-558c-a1f8-bd563702a8c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1.9600" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488587} {:answer/id #uuid "7a1947cb-f049-5278-8b27-3401af91bc08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.1701" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488713} {:answer/id #uuid "cc3e9a65-db77-574a-8530-080325a7bc3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.8808" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488886} {:answer/id #uuid "d1141597-71b6-58dd-a196-da185a8ff0b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2.5758" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488897}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7a1947cb-f049-5278-8b27-3401af91bc08" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2.1701" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488713} :answer-field/id #uuid "9bebb073-a5c7-5042-9111-9520c6e6d7df" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186489102}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e2cf6287-aa23-5f4b-8eb1-c626aabdf157" :question/math-academy-id "q-96960" :question/problem "The table below gives the values of ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ for different values of $p,$ where $p=Φ(z)$ is the cumulative distribution function for the standard normal distribution. Find the value of $z$ such that $P(Z\\le z)=0.015.$\n\n| $\\,p\\,$ | $0.965$ | $0.970$ | $0.975$ | $0.980$ | $0.985$ | $0.990$ | $0.995$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ${Φ}^{-1}(p)$ | $\\,1.8119\\,$ | $\\,1.8808\\,$ | $\\,1.9600\\,$ | $\\,2.0537\\,$ | $\\,2.1701\\,$ | $\\,2.3263\\,$ | $\\,2.5758\\,$ |" :question/worked-solution "From the table, notice that\n\n$$\nP(Z\\le 2.1701)=0.985.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(Z\\ge 2.1701)=1-0.985=0.015.\n$$\n\nBy the symmetry of the standard normal distribution, we have\n\n$$\nΦ(-2.1701)=0.015.\n$$\n\n![](images/47/47a123a730cf175bea1d1887ffdc5a9feb3e1d8f07208c28a9f893a9a1688005.png)\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Φ(-2.1701) & =0.015 \\\\ P(Z\\le -2.1701) & =0.015.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required value of $z$ is $-2.1701.$"}]}
